>> title: Passanda
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: lamb, indian, almond, cream, curry
>> counters: Curry House, One Pot
>> aka: pasanda, lamb passanda, chicken pasanda, pasande, shahi pasanda
>> pairs-with: pilau-rice, naan, ginger-garlic-paste
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — a yogurt sauce with no flour in it breaks at a boil and never comes back, so it stays at the lowest heat you have
>> washing-up: the heavy pot, a bowl to marinate the lamb in

>> step: beat flat, marinate 2 hr
Marinate @lamb leg steaks{2%lb}(900 g; beaten flat between sheets of plastic and cut in strips) with @thick yogurt{3/4%cup}(180 g), @ginger-garlic paste{2%Tbs}(34 g) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} ~marinate{2%hr}.

>> step: sweat 10 min, without colouring it
Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(finely chopped) in @ghee{4%Tbs}(56 g) in a #heavy pot{} under a lid ~fry{10%min}, keeping it pale.

>> step: fry in 2 min
Fry @ground almonds{1/2%cup}(50 g), @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @green cardamom{5%pods}(bruised) and @cinnamon{1%stick}(2-in piece) into @&(~1)softened onion{} ~fry{2%min}.

>> step: simmer 45 min, covered, on the lowest heat
Simmer @&(~3)marinated lamb{} in @&(~1)almond masala{} with @water{1/2%cup}(120 mL), covered and on the lowest heat the ring will hold, ~simmer{45%min}.

>> step: stir in, simmer 5 min
Stir @heavy cream{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @garam masala{1/2%tsp} and @flaked almonds{2%Tbs}(toasted) into @&(~1)pot{} and ~simmer{5%min}.

The leg is beaten flat so it cooks through in three-quarters of an hour and drinks up the yogurt.
